  "readmeFile": "README.md",
  "releaseNotes": "Release candidate 5 corrects how values are written into SPARQL and SQL text. Every literal, language tag and IRI now goes through one serializer for its kind, and a value that cannot be written is refused with an exception naming it rather than written incorrectly. Fixes: a string holding a newline and three apostrophes, a lone carriage return, or several lines ending in an apostrophe was not stored as given; a typed literal stored its quotes as part of its value; an IRI holding a '>' was not refused on every path; on Virtuoso, replacing a graph whose IRI held an apostrophe also deleted the data of other graphs; on Oxigraph, a stored carriage return was read back as a line feed. Upgrading from rc.4: generated SPARQL text double-quotes every literal, and an IRI with a character SPARQL does not allow in one, a malformed blank node label, or a LIMIT, OFFSET or FROM parameter bound to the wrong kind of value now throws on every path, Commit() included. See CHANGELOG.md.",
